        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "generator (NRBG) that utilizes unpredictable physical processes/phenomenon to generate the random numbers. These kinds of RNGs do not require a seed as an input, but are much slower at generating the random number as they first gathers enough physical entropy before they can generate a random number. Additionally, these kinds of RNGs tend to loose entropy over time or with usage. Hence, NRBGs are usually not used for direct generation of a random number. In cryptographic applications, they are mostly used to seed a DRBG. These RNGs are also called true-random number generator (TRNG).",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                169,
                1123,
                327
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    135.0,
